te JD, Heisler M, Horne R, Alexander GC. A conceptually based approach to understanding chronically ill patients&#x02019; responses to medication cost pressures. Soc Sci Med. 2006;62(4):846&#x02013;57. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16095789</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR5"><label>5.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tseng</surname><given-names>C-W</given-names></name><name><surname>Brook</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Keeler</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Steers</surname><given-names>WN</given-names></name><name><surname>Mangione</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cost-lowering strategies used by Medicare beneficiaries who exceed drug benefit caps and have a gap in drug coverage</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2004</year><volume>292</volume><fpage>952</fpage><lpage>960</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.292.8.952</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Tseng C-W, Brook RH, Keeler E, Steers WN, Mangione CM. Cost-lowering strategies used by Medicare beneficiaries who exceed drug benefit caps and have a gap in drug coverage. JAMA. 2004;292:952&#x02013;60. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15328327</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heisler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Piette</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patient strategies to cope with high prescription medication costs: who is cutting back on necessities, increasing debt, or underusing medications</article-title><source>J Behav Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10865-005-2562-z</pub-id></c